1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,841
The disagreement was about whose name would stand on the report, and these two friends had never argued about anything so precious.

2
00:00:07,841 --> 00:00:14,210
“Moreover, the architect is accountable to the client,” the director said.

3
00:00:14,210 --> 00:00:24,508
“Furthermore, a partial account is hazardous to everyone.” Hers was the safer road and yours was the braver one.

4
00:00:24,508 --> 00:00:33,237
The cliff outside the office was occasionally used as a symbol: safe ground above, a dangerous drop below.

5
00:00:33,237 --> 00:00:40,700
“You shrug at the risk because it is the villager who dare not refuse,” the nephew of the client said.

6
00:00:40,700 --> 00:00:46,859
“That is not courage; it is astonishment dressed as bravery.”

7
00:00:46,859 --> 00:00:51,504
The heroic version of the story was also the tragic one.

8
00:00:51,504 --> 00:00:58,497
“An inventor and a bankrupt have the same instinct,” the niece said, shaking her head.

9
00:00:58,497 --> 00:01:11,765
“One is courageous and the other is merely dizzy.” The stainless reputation of the firm was, likewise, a supplement to the argument rather than a part of it.

10
00:01:11,765 --> 00:01:19,454
The peculiarity of the case was that everyone involved was anxious about the same thing and nobody would say it.

11
00:01:19,454 --> 00:01:34,431
“We are terrified of being cowardly,” Maya wrote, “and so we take the riskiest option and call it principle.” The amazing part was how little difference the decision made to the outcome.

12
00:01:34,431 --> 00:01:41,150
The amazement in the room turned to grief when the heroism of the previous year was examined again.

13
00:01:41,150 --> 00:01:47,693
“Besides, a young couple's chances are not yours to spend,” Lin said.

14
00:01:47,693 --> 00:01:53,967
“The value of a value is that it can be considered before the price is paid.”

15
00:01:53,967 --> 00:02:01,756
The compromise was to sign the report together, with the high figure and the low figure on the same page.

16
00:02:01,756 --> 00:02:10,844
The stronger claim would appear first, the weaker one second, and the name of whoever disagreed would be printed beside it.

17
00:02:10,844 --> 00:02:19,503
Moreover, these two things are either risky or hazardous, and everything depends upon whose name is on the top.

18
00:02:19,503 --> 00:02:26,392
The value and the price are too high for a try, although a strong claim can still appear.

19
00:02:26,392 --> 00:02:34,180
A peculiarity of the case is that a partial account is invariably more precious to the author than to the reader.

20
00:02:34,180 --> 00:02:36,485
Whom do we believe?

21
00:02:36,485 --> 00:02:47,475
The answer must be accepted, and a terrific outcome would grieve us; a good carry and a bad number are equal in the same ledger.
